    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41410" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rē-stillo</span></b> , āvi,
		1, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i>, <i>to drop back; to fall back
				in drops.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm.
				2, 287</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae (tuae litterae) mihi quiddam quasi
					animulae restillarunt,</span>”
				<i>have instilled again</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 9, 7, 1</span></i>
			 Orell. <i>N. cr.</i> dub. (B. and K.
			stillarunt).</div>
